### Summary

| Metric | Before | After |
|--------|--------|-------|
| **Aggregate** | 4.95 | **4.96** |
| scout-discovery | 4.82 | **5.00** (+0.18) |
| Other benchmarks | unchanged | — |
| **Benchmarks at ceiling** | 8/11 | **9/11** |

**Change:** Added a **Cross-Host Analysis** section to `scout.md`'s output format, placed between Container Stacks and Security Concerns. It forces the scout to systematically compare services, patch status, backup coverage, single points of failure, and configuration drift across all hosts before finalizing the concern sections. This closes the gap where per-host concern flagging missed patterns that only emerge from cross-host comparison (duplicate Uptime Kuma, systemic patch debt).

**Remaining non-ceiling benchmarks:** runbook-quality (4.86), incident-triage-p1 (4.84), multi-alert-triage (4.89) — all near ceiling with diminishing returns.
